Mutter balances several independent orientation inhibitors: the orientation
lock, display power-save state and whether the built-in panel is managed.
On this tablet the accelerometer appears asynchronously after the monitor.
The managed-panel transition can therefore call uninhibit while the counter is
already zero.  The counter becomes negative and sync_accelerometer_claimed()
is never reached again, although PanelOrientationManaged remains true.

Do not let an unmatched uninhibit underflow the counter.  Treat it as the
already-uninhibited state and resynchronise the D-Bus claim.

SensorProxy must be restarted after deep suspend because Qualcomm's SSC
service is power-collapsed and libssc 0.4.4 does not reconnect an existing QMI
client.  A new SensorProxy name owner invalidates every previous claim.  Reset
Mutter's cached claim state when the new proxy is ready so the normal sync path
always issues a fresh ClaimAccelerometer instead of keeping "undefined".

There is a second ordering race when the accelerometer first appears after the
built-in monitor is already managed.  The first sensor-active signal runs the
initial-orientation compatibility path, which unconditionally adds the
inhibitor that normally represents an as-yet unmanaged panel.  No later
managed-panel transition exists to remove it, so Mutter releases the sensor
immediately after applying one orientation.  Keep that compatibility path when
the panel is still unmanaged, but do not synthesize its inhibitor after the
panel has already become managed.

Finally, the persisted user orientation lock must not share the anonymous
inhibit counter.  If the session starts with orientation-lock=true before the
late accelerometer makes the panel managed, the panel transition's unmatched
uninhibit consumes the user's lock.  The UI still says locked, but Mutter
tracks the sensor until the setting is toggled twice.  The manager already
stores orientation_locked separately, so make it an independent claim
condition and let setting changes resynchronise the claim directly.

diff --git a/src/backends/meta-orientation-manager.c b/src/backends/meta-orientation-manager.c
index 0991fdb..f933fe4 100644
--- a/src/backends/meta-orientation-manager.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-orientation-manager.c
@@ -291 +291,2 @@ sync_accelerometer_claimed (MetaOrientationManager *self)
-  should_claim = self->iio_proxy && self->inhibited_count == 0;
+  should_claim = (self->iio_proxy && self->inhibited_count == 0 &&
+                  !self->orientation_locked);
@@ -341,6 +342,2 @@ orientation_lock_changed (MetaOrientationManager *self)
   self->orientation_locked = orientation_locked;
-
-  if (self->orientation_locked)
-    meta_orientation_manager_inhibit_tracking (self);
-  else
-    meta_orientation_manager_uninhibit_tracking (self);
+  sync_accelerometer_claimed (self);
@@ -361,6 +361,10 @@ iio_proxy_ready (GObject      *source,
       return;
     }
 
+  /* A new D-Bus owner cannot inherit the claim made on the old owner. */
+  self->should_claim = FALSE;
+  self->is_claimed = FALSE;
+
   self->iio_proxy = proxy;
   g_signal_connect_object (self->iio_proxy, "g-properties-changed",
                            G_CALLBACK (iio_properties_changed), self, 0);
@@ -528,6 +532,13 @@ meta_orientation_manager_uninhibit_tracking (MetaOrientationManager *self)
 {
+  if (self->inhibited_count == 0)
+    {
+      g_warning ("Ignoring unmatched orientation tracking uninhibit");
+      sync_accelerometer_claimed (self);
+      return;
+    }
+
   self->inhibited_count--;
 
   if (self->inhibited_count == 0)
     sync_accelerometer_claimed (self);
 }
diff --git a/src/backends/meta-monitor-manager.c b/src/backends/meta-monitor-manager.c
index f37b0a7..d8f74ee 100644
--- a/src/backends/meta-monitor-manager.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-monitor-manager.c
@@ -987,16 +987,20 @@ orientation_changed (MetaMonitorManager *manager)
 
   if (!priv->initial_orient_change_done)
     {
       priv->initial_orient_change_done = TRUE;
-      if (handle_initial_orientation_change (orientation_manager, manager))
+
+      if (!manager->panel_orientation_managed)
         {
+          if (handle_initial_orientation_change (orientation_manager, manager))
+            {
+              meta_orientation_manager_inhibit_tracking (orientation_manager);
+              return;
+            }
+
           meta_orientation_manager_inhibit_tracking (orientation_manager);
-          return;
         }
-
-      meta_orientation_manager_inhibit_tracking (orientation_manager);
     }
 
   if (!manager->panel_orientation_managed)
     return;
